IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sda-common`
IMPORT `taa-procedure`
IMPORT `sda-home`
IMPORT `sda-vehicles`
IMPORT `sda-seat`

-- Stamp Duty Act 1978 (NT) with the Taxation Administration Act 2007 (NT) -- cases for the individual's seat
-- (sda-seat.l4), asked with plain answers as the Interact form would ask them.
--
-- Expected values worked by hand from the deposited reprints (Schedule 1 cl 1(2) and cl 5, s 88(1), s 90D, TAA ss 27,
-- 34-36, 41-43), in an independent calculator (scratchpad au-nt-1/calc/hand.py), never copied from the encoding's output.
-- GENERATED by scratchpad au-nt-1/gen_seat_cases.py, which spells out the long argument lists; the expected values are
-- typed into that script by hand.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Not an official version of either Act; see SOURCE-LICENSE.md.

§ `Cases -- the buyer's and taxpayer's questions`

§§ `Buying a home`

-- $600 000 price, $620 000 value: the dutiable value is the greater (s 4AB).
#ASSERT `What is the dutiable value of my home purchase` 600000 620000 EQUALS 620000
-- A home signed for on 1 March 2026 at $600 000: 4.95%, $29 700.
#ASSERT `How much duty is charged on my home before any concession or exemption` (YMD 2026 3 1) 600000 600000 EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 29700
-- Signed on 1 March 2016: before the deposited Schedule 1.
#ASSERT `How much duty is charged on my home before any concession or exemption` (YMD 2016 3 1) 600000 600000 EQUALS `not covered` `the conveyance or registration is dated before 1 July 2017, when Schedule 1 was last amended (No. 13, 2017); the scale in force before then is not in the deposited reprint`
-- s 88A: the home concessions are open for a contract signed on 30 June 2021, and closed for one signed in 2026.
#ASSERT `Is any Part 5 Division 2 home concession still open for my purchase date` (YMD 2021 6 30)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is any Part 5 Division 2 home concession still open for my purchase date` (YMD 2026 3 1))
-- A first home buyer in 2026, meeting every condition: no concession (s 88A).
#ASSERT `Which home concession do I get, if any` (YMD 2026 3 1) 600000 600000 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no Part 5 Division 2 concession: the Division does not apply to a conveyance first executed after 30 June 2021 (s 88A)`
-- A buyer from interstate on 1 March 2020 at $500 000: the Territory home owner discount, $18 601.
#ASSERT `Which home concession do I get, if any` (YMD 2020 3 1) 500000 500000 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the conveyee is entitled to` `the Territory home owner discount (s 89AAB)` 18601
-- Before 4 May 2010 the home concessions are not in the deposited reprint (s 102).
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to this home concession, setting aside s 90B` `the first home owner concession (s 89)` (YMD 2009 3 1) 600000 600000 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not covered here` `the conveyance was first executed before 4 May 2010; the home concessions as they stood before the 2010 amendments (s 102) are not in the deposited reprint`
-- A senior selling a Territory home and buying another on 1 March 2020: entitled to the senior concession.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to this home concession, setting aside s 90B` `the senior, pensioner and carer concession (s 89A)` (YMD 2020 3 1) 600000 600000 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes, apart from s 90B: only the one concession of greatest benefit can be had`
-- The Territory home owner discount for a 2026 contract: no.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to this home concession, setting aside s 90B` `the Territory home owner discount (s 89AAB)` (YMD 2026 3 1) 600000 600000 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no`
-- A house-and-land contract with a building contractor, 1 March 2026, $650 000: exempt (s 90D); nothing to pay.
#ASSERT `Is my purchase of a new home from a building contractor exempt` (YMD 2026 3 1) 650000 650000 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `How much duty must I pay on my home` (YMD 2026 3 1) 650000 650000 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 0
-- The same contract signed on 1 July 2027: the window has closed; $32 175.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my purchase of a new home from a building contractor exempt` (YMD 2027 7 1) 650000 650000 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `How much duty must I pay on my home` (YMD 2027 7 1) 650000 650000 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 32175
-- An established home in 2026 at $600 000: $29 700 to pay.
#ASSERT `How much duty must I pay on my home` (YMD 2026 3 1) 600000 600000 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 29700
-- The interstate buyer of 1 March 2020 at $500 000: $23 928.6025 less $18 601, rounded down to 5 cents: $5 327.60.
#ASSERT `How much duty must I pay on my home` (YMD 2020 3 1) 500000 500000 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 5327.6
-- Two joint owners of an $800 000 home transfer it to one of them in 2026: duty on a half share, $16 514.3056, plus $5,
-- rounded down to 5 cents (TAA s 27): $16 519.30 (finding 21).
#ASSERT `How much duty is charged on a transfer between joint owners` (YMD 2026 3 1) 800000 0.5 EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 16519.3
#ASSERT `Who must pay the duty` `a conveyance` EQUALS `the conveyee (s 50(a))`
#ASSERT `Within how many days after signing must I lodge my transfer` EQUALS 60
#ASSERT `By how many days after signing must I pay the duty` 0 EQUALS 60
#ASSERT `By how many days after signing must I pay the duty` 90 EQUALS 90

§§ `Living in the home`

#ASSERT `Within how many months after possession must I start living in the home` `a home is built on the land` 0 0 EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `Within how many months after possession must I start living in the home` `no home yet: the conveyees are owner builders or have a comprehensive home building contract` 30 0 EQUALS 42
#ASSERT `For how many months in a row must I live in the home` EQUALS 6
-- Both buyers of the s 90D home will not move in: notice within 30 days, or up to 50 penalty units.
#ASSERT `Must I tell the Commissioner that I will not live in the home` `s 90D(5) -- exemption for a new home from a building contractor` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: written notice to the Commissioner within this many days after it first becomes apparent, or a fine of up to this many penalty units` 30 50
-- The co-buyer has already told the Commissioner; or only one of two buyers moves out: no notice from me.
#ASSERT `Must I tell the Commissioner that I will not live in the home` `s 90D(5) -- exemption for a new home from a building contractor` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no notice is required of me`
#ASSERT `Must I tell the Commissioner that I will not live in the home` `s 90D(5) -- exemption for a new home from a building contractor` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no notice is required of me`
-- After the failure the Commissioner must reassess under s 90D(8); there is no such duty under s 89AA.
#ASSERT `Must the Commissioner reassess my duty because I did not live in the home` `s 90D(5) -- exemption for a new home from a building contractor` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the Commissioner reassess my duty because I did not live in the home` `s 89AA(6) -- first home owner discount` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- The grant paid after the senior concession or the Territory discount: the concession goes (ss 90A(2), 90AB(2)); not after s 89.
#ASSERT `Must the Commissioner take my concession back because the grant was paid` `the senior, pensioner and carer concession (s 89A)` TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the Commissioner take my concession back because the grant was paid` `the Territory home owner discount (s 89AAB)` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the Commissioner take my concession back because the grant was paid` `the first home owner concession (s 89)` TRUE)

§§ `Exempt transfers`

#ASSERT `Is my property settlement with my former partner exempt` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) `a Family Court order under Part VIII or VIIIAB of the Family Law Act` (YMD 2027 2 15) TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my property settlement with my former partner exempt` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) `a Family Court order under Part VIII or VIIIAB of the Family Law Act` (YMD 2027 3 2) TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Must the Commissioner refund the duty I paid on my settlement` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) `a binding financial agreement under Part VIIIA or VIIIAB of the Family Law Act` (YMD 2026 9 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the transfer to me from a deceased estate exempt` TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my gift to a Special Disability Trust exempt` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my gift to a Special Disability Trust exempt` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Is the transfer of our home between me and my spouse exempt` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE

§§ `Registering a vehicle`

#ASSERT `What is the dutiable value of my vehicle` (YMD 2026 3 1) TRUE 30000 1500 0 0 FALSE EQUALS 31500
#ASSERT `How much duty must I pay to register my vehicle` (YMD 2026 3 1) TRUE 30000 1500 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 945
-- Moving to the Territory with my own car (last registered in my name): exempt.
#ASSERT `Is my vehicle registration exempt from duty` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `exempt: re-registration in the name of the person it was last registered to (item 23(a))`
#ASSERT `How much duty must I pay to register my vehicle` (YMD 2026 3 1) TRUE 30000 1500 0 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 0
-- A $60 000 electric car on 1 March 2026: $1 800 less $1 500, $300.
#ASSERT `How much duty must I pay to register my vehicle` (YMD 2026 3 1) TRUE 60000 0 0 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 300
-- A 4.6 t caravan bought for $20 000 is not exempt: $600.
#ASSERT `How much duty must I pay to register my vehicle` (YMD 2026 3 1) TRUE 20000 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 4.6 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 600
#ASSERT `Must I lodge a declaration to claim my vehicle exemption or concession` `an item 23 exemption`
#ASSERT NOT (`Must I lodge a declaration to claim my vehicle exemption or concession` `the s 92A electric vehicle concession`)
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined over vehicle duty, in penalty units` EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `Within how many days must I notify the price I received for my vehicle` EQUALS 14
#ASSERT `Will my vehicle duty be refunded if the sale is cancelled` TRUE TRUE TRUE

§§ `Challenging an assessment or a grant decision`

#ASSERT `How much of this decision can I object to` `an assessment or reassessment of duty` TRUE 20000 25000 EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `Within how many days must I object` FALSE 0 EQUALS 60
#ASSERT `Within how many days must I object` TRUE 90 EQUALS 90
#ASSERT `Can my late objection still be accepted` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `Where can I take my objection next` `a first home owner grant decision` `the objection is disallowed` EQUALS `to NTCAT for review only`
#ASSERT `Where can I take my objection next` `an assessment or reassessment of duty` `the objection is allowed in part only` EQUALS `to NTCAT for review, or to the Supreme Court on appeal, but not both`
#ASSERT `Within how many days must I apply for review or appeal` EQUALS 60
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my objection stop the duty being collected`)
-- Assessed 1 March 2020; reassessed 2 March 2026 for a failure to occupy: allowed (s 21(4)(c)); for the grant after the Territory discount: not; on my written application within 5 years: allowed.
#ASSERT `Can the Commissioner still reassess my duty` (YMD 2020 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 2) FALSE FALSE `a failure to occupy the home (ss 89(4), 89AAB(4), 89A(6), 90(4), 90D(8))` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the Commissioner still reassess my duty` (YMD 2020 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 2) FALSE FALSE `the first home owner grant, after the Territory home owner discount (s 90AB)` FALSE)
#ASSERT `Can the Commissioner still reassess my duty` (YMD 2020 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 2) FALSE FALSE `any other reason` TRUE

§§ `Penalty tax and interest`

#ASSERT `How much penalty tax can I be charged` 10000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 2500
#ASSERT `What is the least penalty tax after a reduction for cooperation or disclosure` 10000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS 500
-- Finding 23: I hindered the assessment but concealed nothing: 75%, $7 500, and the 80% reduction is still open, $1 500.
-- Had I concealed information, there is no reduction: $7 500.
#ASSERT `How much penalty tax can I be charged` 10000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 7500
#ASSERT `What is the least penalty tax after a reduction for cooperation or disclosure` 10000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS 1500
#ASSERT `What is the least penalty tax after a reduction for cooperation or disclosure` 10000 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS 7500
#ASSERT `Within how many days must I pay penalty tax` 7 EQUALS 14
-- Interest: the market rates are made-up inputs. Within one financial year: 12 500 x 12.35% x 73/365 = $308.75.
#ASSERT `How much interest is charged on my unpaid duty` 10000 2500 4.35 0 (YMD 2026 7 1) (YMD 2026 9 12) EQUALS `the interest, in dollars, is` 308.75
-- Finding 22: across 30 June 2026, 30 days at 12.10% and 30 days at 12.35% on $10 000: 73 350/365 = $200.9589..., $200.95.
#ASSERT `How much interest is charged on my unpaid duty` 10000 0 4.10 4.35 (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 7 31) EQUALS `the interest, in dollars, is` 200.95
-- Unpaid from 1 June 2025 to 1 August 2026: three financial years, more than the two rates asked for, so not covered.
#ASSERT `How much interest is charged on my unpaid duty` 10000 0 4.10 4.35 (YMD 2025 6 1) (YMD 2026 8 1) EQUALS `the interest is not covered` `the tax default runs into a financial year for which no market interest rate is given; the market interest rate is set for each financial year (TAA s 35(2)) and is not in the deposited texts`
